WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:03.567
-Welcome, welcome, welcome
to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:03.567 --> 00:00:05.167
You're here. You made it.
Thank you for watching.

00:00:05.167 --> 00:00:08.033
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:08.033 --> 00:00:11.167
Well, guys,
it's Halloween weekend.

00:00:11.167 --> 00:00:13.601
-Yes!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:13.601 --> 00:00:15.200
-And get this --
here in New York City,

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:17.934
it's gonna be 80 degrees.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:17.934 --> 00:00:19.901
80 degrees.
But everyone's mom

00:00:19.901 --> 00:00:21.868
will still make them wear
a jacket over their costume.

00:00:21.868 --> 00:00:24.234
[ Laughter ]
"I don't want you to be chilly.

00:00:24.234 --> 00:00:25.968
Everyone knows you're
Spider-Man."

00:00:25.968 --> 00:00:28.634
[ Laughter ]

00:00:28.634 --> 00:00:30.000
You know it's too hot

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:32.033
when you see houses
covered in fried eggs.

00:00:32.033 --> 00:00:34.200
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:36.033
-You know it's too hot
when you bob for apples

00:00:36.033 --> 00:00:38.501
and just kind of stay there.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:38.501 --> 00:00:39.701
Let's get to some news.

00:00:39.701 --> 00:00:41.801
I saw that President Biden's
approval rating

00:00:41.801 --> 00:00:45.200
among his fellow Democrats
just dropped 11 points

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:47.634
to a record low of 75%.

00:00:47.634 --> 00:00:49.033
[ Audience "Oohs" ]

00:00:49.033 --> 00:00:50.367
-Yikes.
Even Jill is like,

00:00:50.367 --> 00:00:52.267
"So tell me more about
this Robert Kennedy fella."

00:00:52.267 --> 00:00:54.100
[ Laughter ]

00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:55.801
If Biden becomes
any less popular,

00:00:55.801 --> 00:00:57.734
Republicans might elect him
speaker of the House.

00:00:57.734 --> 00:00:59.934
-Oh!
[ Audience groans ]

00:00:59.934 --> 00:01:03.534
-That's correct.
Yeah, Biden's down to 75%.

00:01:03.534 --> 00:01:05.167
On the bright side,
he gets to tell people

00:01:05.167 --> 00:01:06.901
that he's in his mid 70s again.
-Aww.

00:01:06.901 --> 00:01:08.834
[ Laughter ]

00:01:08.834 --> 00:01:10.868
When Biden asks how
he could boost his numbers,

00:01:10.868 --> 00:01:13.133
his staff said, "Try walking
from the car to the plane

00:01:13.133 --> 00:01:14.834
without making people think,
"Oh, God, oh, God,

00:01:14.834 --> 00:01:15.834
oh, God, oh God!"

00:01:15.834 --> 00:01:19.200
[ Laughter ]

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:21.901
It's like, "Is he walking --
Is he walking on skates?

00:01:21.901 --> 00:01:24.734
Is he wearing ice skates
in the parking lot?"

00:01:24.734 --> 00:01:27.567
Don't worry. Biden has a way
to boost his popularity. Yeah.

00:01:27.567 --> 00:01:29.133
He's gonna become
pickleball partners

00:01:29.133 --> 00:01:32.167
with the Golden Bachelor.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:32.167 --> 00:01:33.701
No, actually,
this is gonna help him.

00:01:33.701 --> 00:01:36.467
He's now rebranding himself
as Joe Biden: Taylor's Version.

00:01:36.467 --> 00:01:37.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:37.667 --> 00:01:40.033
That's how you do it.
That's how you do it.

00:01:40.033 --> 00:01:44.501
Smart.
[ Cheering continues ]

00:01:44.501 --> 00:01:46.133
Some --
Some movie news.

00:01:46.133 --> 00:01:49.000
Today, the new horror movie
"Five Nights at Freddy's"

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:53.567
hit theaters and started
streaming on Peacock.

00:01:53.567 --> 00:01:56.267
Yeah, it is being called
the "Casablanca" of movies

00:01:56.267 --> 00:01:58.067
featuring giant robot animals
in a pizzeria.

00:01:58.067 --> 00:01:59.467
[ Laughter ]

00:01:59.467 --> 00:02:02.968
It is a horror movie that is set
in a place like Chuck E. Cheese.

00:02:02.968 --> 00:02:04.267
Yeah. It's terrifying.

00:02:04.267 --> 00:02:06.100
In one scene, they shine
a black light on the ball pit.

00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:08.501
-Oh!
-Eee.

00:02:08.501 --> 00:02:11.200
Hey, did you guys see this?
The magician David Copperfield

00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:13.901
just announced plans
to make the Moon disappear.

00:02:13.901 --> 00:02:15.067
[ Laughter ]

00:02:15.067 --> 00:02:17.567
Yeah, it's an amazing trick
he calls daytime.

00:02:17.567 --> 00:02:19.334
[ Laughter ]
Un...

00:02:21.067 --> 00:02:23.000
[ Laughter ]

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:25.834
Yep. David Copperfield will
make the Moon disappear.

00:02:25.834 --> 00:02:27.200
Yeah.
Then for his next trick,

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:30.200
he threatened to pull
a rabbit out of Uranus.

00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:31.334
-And that's --
-Hey-o!

00:02:31.334 --> 00:02:33.067
-What? What?
[ Rimshot ]

00:02:33.067 --> 00:02:36.067
-What?!
-Guys, I read that

00:02:36.067 --> 00:02:37.701
since people started
going back to work,

00:02:37.701 --> 00:02:41.467
the makers of Axe deodorant
have seen a 15% surge in sales.

00:02:41.467 --> 00:02:43.200
-Ooh.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:44.968
-Of course, Axe body spray
is very popular

00:02:44.968 --> 00:02:46.801
because it can also
be used as mace.

00:02:46.801 --> 00:02:48.400
[ Laughter ]

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:51.334
Some more business news.
For the first time in 50 years,

00:02:51.334 --> 00:02:54.234
Cup Noodles is making a change
to their cups

00:02:54.234 --> 00:02:56.868
by switching from styrofoam
to paper.

00:02:56.868 --> 00:03:00.534
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:00.534 --> 00:03:03.467
Not to be alarmed, though, the
noodles will still be styrofoam.

00:03:03.467 --> 00:03:06.501
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:06.501 --> 00:03:09.267
[ Rimshot ]

00:03:09.267 --> 00:03:12.300
Yeah, they saw all the success
of paper straws and thought,

00:03:12.300 --> 00:03:14.200
"Let's try it
with boiling hot soup."

00:03:14.200 --> 00:03:16.200
[ Laughter ]

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:17.534
I had a great night
last night.

00:03:17.534 --> 00:03:20.467
I went out to, uh --
I went to Carbone.

00:03:20.467 --> 00:03:21.701
-Ooh.
-Yeah.

00:03:21.701 --> 00:03:24.567
So I went with a my friend
Mike Birbiglia,

00:03:24.567 --> 00:03:27.434
a very funny comedian, and we're
talking about stand-up,

00:03:27.434 --> 00:03:28.968
and he's like -- he's like,
"Yeah, you should

00:03:28.968 --> 00:03:31.300
do stand-up again."
And I go, yeah, I know,

00:03:31.300 --> 00:03:34.868
because I did start my career
in stand-up, and I go,

00:03:34.868 --> 00:03:37.501
I just haven't been on stage
in probably 10 years.

00:03:37.501 --> 00:03:38.868
And, you know,
Chris Rock tells me

00:03:38.868 --> 00:03:41.534
I should do stand-up again.
And I go, "Yeah, I know.

00:03:41.534 --> 00:03:43.100
I just got to get an act
and blah, blah, blah."

00:03:43.100 --> 00:03:44.601
He goes, "You should go
to the Comedy Cellar

00:03:44.601 --> 00:03:46.200
and just go up," and I go,

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:48.234
"I know, I know.
So I don't have an act."

00:03:48.234 --> 00:03:50.667
And he's like,
"Let's just walk down there

00:03:50.667 --> 00:03:53.601
and just -- just break
the ice of -- just the myth

00:03:53.601 --> 00:03:55.467
of just going on stage
at the thing."

00:03:55.467 --> 00:03:56.868
I go, "Yeah, okay."

00:03:56.868 --> 00:03:59.834
So I went,
and it's an amazing club.

00:03:59.834 --> 00:04:01.133
I go, "Yeah,
I totally remember it."

00:04:01.133 --> 00:04:02.667
And you go down the stairs
and the whole thing,

00:04:02.667 --> 00:04:06.133
and there's a great comedian,
Tina Friml, was on.

00:04:06.133 --> 00:04:08.334
So I went and watched her set.
It was awesome.

00:04:08.334 --> 00:04:09.767
And then I go, "All right,
I'm gonna leave."

00:04:09.767 --> 00:04:11.234
And I went in the hallway,
and Chris Rock

00:04:11.234 --> 00:04:13.934
is sitting on the stairs.
He's like...

00:04:13.934 --> 00:04:17.234
"I knew you'd come back.
I knew you'd come back.

00:04:17.234 --> 00:04:18.801
You have to come back
to stand-up.

00:04:18.801 --> 00:04:20.167
You've got to do it, man.
I knew it.

00:04:20.167 --> 00:04:21.734
I knew you'd come back."
I go -- and I felt

00:04:21.734 --> 00:04:23.234
like the comedy gods
were just telling me,

00:04:23.234 --> 00:04:25.567
like, "Yeah,
you should do stand-up again."

00:04:25.567 --> 00:04:27.834
So I go, "Yeah."
I go, "Are you going up?"

00:04:27.834 --> 00:04:29.801
And he's like, "Yeah,
maybe I'll go up."

00:04:29.801 --> 00:04:32.434
So he surprised the audience.
Chris Rock gets up,

00:04:32.434 --> 00:04:34.400
surprised the audience,
and destroys.

00:04:34.400 --> 00:04:35.734
He's unbelievable.

00:04:35.734 --> 00:04:38.601
And so then I went up
to give him a bottle of water,

00:04:38.601 --> 00:04:41.200
like as a goof,
and everyone started clapping.

00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:44.033
And then he goes, he took
the microphone, and he goes...

00:04:44.033 --> 00:04:45.634
[ Laughter ]

00:04:45.634 --> 00:04:47.033
I was like, "Wow."

00:04:47.033 --> 00:04:49.801
So I did stand-up
for the first time last night

00:04:49.801 --> 00:04:51.300
in 10 years.
-Wow!

00:04:51.300 --> 00:04:55.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:55.133 --> 00:04:58.000
-It was unbelievable.
I totally remembered it.

00:04:58.000 --> 00:05:00.534
It was super fun.
It was great.

00:05:00.534 --> 00:05:01.701
I was like --
I don't even know --

00:05:01.701 --> 00:05:02.834
I don't know what I was
talking about.

00:05:02.834 --> 00:05:04.367
We just made it --
He made me so comfortable

00:05:04.367 --> 00:05:06.534
up there.
But I remember, like,

00:05:06.534 --> 00:05:08.934
"Oh, yeah,
it's so fun to be onstage."

00:05:08.934 --> 00:05:11.434
And when a joke works,
the crowd loves it.

00:05:11.434 --> 00:05:14.033
I mean, like, the monologue.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:14.033 --> 00:05:15.801
-And when it doesn't.
-And when it doesn't work,

00:05:15.801 --> 00:05:18.801
you know, it's silence,
and, uh...

00:05:18.801 --> 00:05:20.667
No, but I do remember that.

00:05:20.667 --> 00:05:23.100
The room gets hot, you know,

00:05:23.100 --> 00:05:24.534
when you tell a good joke,
and then it's like...

00:05:24.534 --> 00:05:26.100
And then it like,
comes down to room temperature.

00:05:26.100 --> 00:05:28.067
I loved it.
Anyways, I got the bug,

00:05:28.067 --> 00:05:29.767
and I wanted
to thank thank Chris.

00:05:29.767 --> 00:05:32.367
Thanks, Mike.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:32.367 --> 00:05:34.734
Thank you, Comedy Cellar.

00:05:34.734 --> 00:05:36.434
I got to --
I'll work on an act.

00:05:36.434 --> 00:05:37.601
-Yeah.
-I'm gonna work on an act,

00:05:37.601 --> 00:05:38.901
and I'll be out there,
because I want to go out

00:05:38.901 --> 00:05:40.100
around the country.

00:05:40.100 --> 00:05:41.567
I want to say hi to everybody
and all the fans.

00:05:41.567 --> 00:05:43.534
I love meeting people, and I
think it's gonna be fun.

00:05:43.534 --> 00:05:45.334
I'll do it.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:45.334 --> 00:05:46.801
So, it's Halloween.
Give me a couple of months.

00:05:46.801 --> 00:05:47.901
I'll work on something.
-Couple months.

00:05:47.901 --> 00:05:49.100
-All right, good.
Right now, though,

00:05:49.100 --> 00:05:50.834
if you guys don't mind,

00:05:50.834 --> 00:05:52.868
do you mind if I write out
some thank-you notes right now?

00:05:52.868 --> 00:05:53.968
Is that cool with you?

00:05:53.968 --> 00:05:56.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:56.467 --> 00:05:58.501
James -- James, can I get some
thank you note

00:05:58.501 --> 00:05:59.868
writing music, please?

00:05:59.868 --> 00:06:01.133
♪♪

00:06:01.133 --> 00:06:03.634
-Oh.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:03.634 --> 00:06:06.868
-Oh, he's -- he's psyched.
-Yeah.

00:06:06.868 --> 00:06:08.701
-Guess he's got a couple
Red Bulls before the show.

00:06:08.701 --> 00:06:10.801
-Wow.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:10.801 --> 00:06:12.667
Eee!

00:06:12.667 --> 00:06:14.033
♪♪

00:06:14.033 --> 00:06:17.400
-Thank you, new speaker
of the House Mike Johnson,

00:06:17.400 --> 00:06:19.501
for being the first person
to win an election

00:06:19.501 --> 00:06:21.000
with the slogan,
"You've seen the best.

00:06:21.000 --> 00:06:22.367
Now vote for the rest."

00:06:22.367 --> 00:06:26.000
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]
Come on.

00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:29.767
Why not?
-Why not, man?

00:06:29.767 --> 00:06:31.334
♪♪

00:06:31.334 --> 00:06:33.234
-Thank you, Reese's Pieces,

00:06:33.234 --> 00:06:34.834
for making me see
which one of my friends

00:06:34.834 --> 00:06:36.400
can't pronounce Reese's.

00:06:36.400 --> 00:06:37.534
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:06:37.534 --> 00:06:39.701
Oh, "Reesie's."

00:06:39.701 --> 00:06:41.701
-Reese's.
-"Reesie's" Piece --

00:06:41.701 --> 00:06:44.300
"Reesie's Piecies."
-"Reese's Piecies."

00:06:44.300 --> 00:06:45.701
-Reese's Pieces.

00:06:45.701 --> 00:06:47.567
-Reesie's Piecies feces.

00:06:47.567 --> 00:06:49.000
[ Laughter ]

00:06:49.000 --> 00:06:50.300
♪♪

00:06:50.300 --> 00:06:52.901
-Thank you,
walking through a spider web,

00:06:52.901 --> 00:06:54.968
for turning me
into a black belt in karate.

00:06:54.968 --> 00:06:59.534
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:59.534 --> 00:07:02.000
-Whoa!

00:07:05.467 --> 00:07:06.834
♪♪

00:07:06.834 --> 00:07:09.801
-Thank you, TikTok's
planned music festival,

00:07:09.801 --> 00:07:11.934
for promising to be
a fun gathering of people

00:07:11.934 --> 00:07:13.801
staring at their phones
for five hours.

00:07:13.801 --> 00:07:16.868
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:07:22.934 --> 00:07:24.334
♪♪

00:07:24.334 --> 00:07:27.534
Thank you, Frankenstein,
for looking like the Hulk

00:07:27.534 --> 00:07:29.901
after dealing with Spectrum
customer service.

00:07:29.901 --> 00:07:33.868
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:07:33.868 --> 00:07:35.634
-Wow.
-What?

00:07:35.634 --> 00:07:37.601
-Spectrum?

00:07:37.601 --> 00:07:39.033
Are you gonna send that
to Frankenstein?

00:07:39.033 --> 00:07:40.334
-I have no idea.

00:07:40.334 --> 00:07:41.601
-So you're thanking
Frankenstein with that?

00:07:41.601 --> 00:07:42.868
-I don't know
who I'm thanking again.

00:07:42.868 --> 00:07:44.801
Am I thanking the Hulk?
-Thanking Frankenstein.

00:07:44.801 --> 00:07:46.133
-Oh, wait.
I'm thanking Frankenstein.

00:07:46.133 --> 00:07:47.767
-Yeah, Frankenstein.
-He looks like --

00:07:47.767 --> 00:07:49.567
Because he looks like the Hulk

00:07:49.567 --> 00:07:51.634
after dealing with
Spectrum customer --

00:07:51.634 --> 00:07:53.334
[ Laughter ]

00:07:53.334 --> 00:07:54.434
I don't know, man.

00:07:54.434 --> 00:07:55.501
-You got to put it
in the mail, right?

00:07:55.501 --> 00:07:57.667
-Hey, man, you got to do it.

00:07:57.667 --> 00:07:59.367
-Yeah. Come on, Frank.
-Come on, man.

00:07:59.367 --> 00:08:01.667
Come on, Frank.

00:08:01.667 --> 00:08:03.701
-Frankie.

00:08:03.701 --> 00:08:05.601
-Frankie boy.
-Come on, boy!

00:08:05.601 --> 00:08:07.534
You been dealing
with Spectrum customer service!

00:08:07.534 --> 00:08:09.467
-Whoo-ooh!

00:08:09.467 --> 00:08:13.334
[ Laughter ]

00:08:13.334 --> 00:08:14.467
-Are you going to send
that one?

00:08:14.467 --> 00:08:16.167
-What's that?
[ Laughter ]

00:08:16.167 --> 00:08:17.501
-That other one,
you're gonna send it in?

00:08:17.501 --> 00:08:19.200
-The other one?
Uh, yeah, maybe.

00:08:19.200 --> 00:08:20.400
I might send it in,
I might not.

00:08:20.400 --> 00:08:21.734
I don't even know at this point.
-Just checking.

00:08:21.734 --> 00:08:23.100
-I don't know.
Thanks for checking, though.

00:08:23.100 --> 00:08:24.200
-Well, I want to make sure
you're okay.

00:08:24.200 --> 00:08:25.601
-Yeah, I will.

00:08:25.601 --> 00:08:28.501
-[ Breathes deeply ]

00:08:28.501 --> 00:08:29.868
[ Laughter ]

00:08:29.868 --> 00:08:31.200
♪♪

00:08:31.200 --> 00:08:34.467
-Thank you, "It's the
Great Pumpkin, Charlie Brown,"

00:08:34.467 --> 00:08:37.033
for the scariest moment
in any "Peanuts" special,

00:08:37.033 --> 00:08:39.767
when you realize Sally is
just Charlie Brown in a wig.

00:08:39.767 --> 00:08:42.534
[ Laughter, cheers, applause ]

00:08:42.534 --> 00:08:44.200
♪♪

00:08:44.200 --> 00:08:46.934
-What?

00:08:46.934 --> 00:08:49.033
[ Applause ]

00:08:49.033 --> 00:08:50.400
-[ Imitating "Peanuts" teacher
speaking ]

00:08:50.400 --> 00:08:54.367
-Probably Linus and Lucy.
-Yeah.

00:08:54.367 --> 00:08:55.701
♪♪

00:08:55.701 --> 00:08:58.467
Thank you,
fun-size candy,

00:08:58.467 --> 00:09:01.133
for being the short kings
of the chocolate world.

00:09:01.133 --> 00:09:02.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:02.634 --> 00:09:04.200
[ Both laugh ]

00:09:04.200 --> 00:09:07.200
-Wow!
Big fans of short kings.

00:09:07.200 --> 00:09:09.567
[ Laughing ]

00:09:09.567 --> 00:09:11.167
♪♪

00:09:11.167 --> 00:09:14.501
-Thank you, candy corn,
for being the most delicious way

00:09:14.501 --> 00:09:16.133
to eat a candle.
There you have it, everybody.

00:09:16.133 --> 00:09:17.634
Those are my thank-you notes.

